# generated harness evidence
harness/evidence/

# design-review captures — binaries + PII-shaped; reproduce via harness/archive/capture-route.ts
# (archived 2026-08-18 · mootech-fe#321 — the dir stays here because that is where the tool writes), don't commit
harness/captures/

# raw image sources — ฟีม drops originals here; `npm run assets:optimize` writes the committed .webp to public/
# ignore the raw images themselves, but KEEP the README so the dir + how-to is tracked
assets-src/*
!assets-src/README.md

# test-env secrets (passkey etc.) — never commit
testenv/env/*.env

# first-frame / shift evidence — a screencast run writes hundreds of PNGs (~350MB per run). The NUMBERS
# are the evidence and they live in the PR body; the frames are reproducible with the command beside them.
# (harness/out itself still tracks the small curated shots earlier PRs committed.)
# ONE ignored root for every run dump. The first version of this listed dirs by name and the very next
# card's runs (--out ctl-nav, p4-normal, exp-400 …) walked straight past it — a rule that has to be
# updated every time it is used is a rule that will be forgotten exactly once. The harnesses now default
# their --out under here, so a new run name cannot leak 350MB into a commit.
harness/out/_frames/

# pixel evidence from a harness run (#417, ฟีม 2026-08-23) — screenshots a harness takes to prove a
# layout claim are TEST OUTPUT, not something the app serves. The NUMBERS are the evidence and they
# live in the PR body; the picture is reproducible with the command printed beside them.
# This root exists because the rule above could not reach the harnesses: six of them spelled
# `harness/pixel-proof/` out in their own source, so nothing here knew they existed, and they kept
# committing. #414 alone added 23 PNGs / 9.91 MB, against a `pixel-proof/` already at 75 files /
# 19.24 MB inside a 488 MB `.git`. Nobody skipped a step — the path was simply not a value anyone owned.
# It is one now: `harness/evidence-dir.mjs` returns it, all six import it, and a seventh harness gets
# the rule by importing rather than by remembering it.
# `harness/pixel-proof/` itself stays TRACKED on purpose: 75 files are already in history, `#418` cites
# one by SHA, and deleting them would break links without shrinking anything. We stop it growing.
# (`harness/out/_frames/` above predates this and still serves the screencast harnesses that point at
#  it. Two roots is one more than the lesson wants — folding them together is worth its own card.)
harness/.tmp/

# Serwist PWA build output (#285) — regenerated by `next build`, never commit
public/sw.js
public/sw.js.map
public/swe-worker-*.js
